Hello all,

Since I had something to say about the staging patches for Hyper-V, I
figure I'd start to help out a bit. These next 8 patches are strictly
style related, and are done in what I hope is the careful, methodical
style of Greg K-H. I've read Documentation/CodingStyle and am surprised
by how much of it I agree with (and those that I don't, I still do).

I have some ideas on more substantive changes, but since I've never
submitted Linux kernel patches before, I'm staring slowly. I welcome
feedback on whether I'm submitting patches in a useful manner (right place,
right way, right form), but I do ask that you please be gentle. I do
learn fast.

If this works, I'll dig in a bit more.

Steve

